# PROVEN — environment template. COPY to `.env` and fill in. Never commit `.env`.
#
#     copy .env.example .env        (Windows)
#
# EVERYTHING BELOW IS OPTIONAL. The product runs, all 817 tests pass, and every
# finding, figure and score is produced without any of it. What a key adds is the AI
# layer: semantic retrieval instead of lexical, model-proposed mechanism identification
# on wordings nobody has hand-mapped, plain-language explanations, and the Ask Pulse
# copilot. What it does not add is authority — no model decides coverage, resolves
# precedence, computes a settlement figure, sets an evidence class or moves the score,
# and `tests/test_ai_layer.py` asserts that against the import graph.
#
# With no key the interface says DETERMINISTIC_ONLY and names lexical retrieval as the
# mode in use. That is deliberate: a product that silently falls back while implying
# semantic search is making the kind of unstated claim this system exists to refuse.

# Your OpenAI key. Read by config.py at import. Never logged, never served by any
# endpoint — tests/test_ai_layer.py::test_no_endpoint_leaks_the_api_key sweeps for it.
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

# Optional model overrides. The defaults are small and cheap on purpose: the model's
# job here is extraction and phrasing, not reasoning about money, so a frontier model
# would buy nothing.
# PROVEN_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# PROVEN_EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small

# Seconds before an AI call is abandoned and the deterministic path answers instead.
# A slow provider must degrade to a working page, not a hung one.
# PROVEN_AI_TIMEOUT=25

# ── LIVE external data sources (Priority 1) ─────────────────────────────────
# OFF by default. When set to 1, the Sentinel and Discovery agents and the drift index
# make REAL outbound calls to Singapore government open-data endpoints:
#   - data.gov.sg rainfall + 24h forecast   (Sentinel weather)
#   - SingStat Table Builder M211251         (Sentinel cost index + drift)
#   - ACRA company register (data.gov.sg)    (Discovery)
#   - OneMap geocoding                        (premises → nearest rainfall station)
# Each call has a 15s timeout and falls back to a labelled DEMO_FIXTURE on failure — a
# fixture is NEVER rendered as live. Leave this UNSET when running the test suite: the
# tests must not require a network round trip, and they mock the HTTP layer instead.
#
# Enable it for a live demo without editing .env, e.g. (PowerShell):
#     $env:PROVEN_LIVE_SOURCES="1"; python -m uvicorn proven.api:app --port 8000
# PROVEN_LIVE_SOURCES=1

# ── The business's own website (Discovery) ──────────────────────────────────
# Hock Lee Foods is a fictional company, so `hockleefoods.com.sg` does not resolve and
# every live Discovery run against it used to die on DNS — which meant the one capability
# the agent exists to show, noticing a change the business published but never told its
# insurer, could not be demonstrated at all.
#
# So the repo ships that website as a SEPARATE process and points Discovery at it. What
# the product does to it is a genuine outbound HTTP GET: real request, real HTML, real
# parsing, real grounding gate. Only the company is a stand-in.
#
# Start it in its own terminal, alongside the app:
#     python demo-site/site.py                  # -> http://127.0.0.1:8100
#
# Then open http://127.0.0.1:8100/operator to change the business live — open a branch,
# change the team size — and watch the app notice on its next check. A real deployment
# points this at the customer's actual URL and nothing else changes.
# PROVEN_DEMO_SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8100

# ── Email notifications ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UNSET by default, and the behaviour with nothing configured is deliberate rather than a
# degraded mode: every notification is still COMPOSED IN FULL and written to an outbox you
# can open and read in the app, marked NO_MAIL_SERVER. Nothing claims to have been
# delivered when it was not. A "sent!" toast with nothing on the wire is exactly the kind
# of unstated claim this product refuses to make about anything else.
#
# Set both HOST and FROM to send for real. Port 465 uses SMTP_SSL; anything else uses
# STARTTLS unless PROVEN_SMTP_TLS=0. Credentials are optional — some relays do not want
# them. `mailer.status()` reports whether a password is PRESENT and never what it is.
# PROVEN_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# PROVEN_SMTP_PORT=587
# PROVEN_SMTP_USER=you@example.com
# PROVEN_SMTP_PASSWORD=an-app-specific-password
# PROVEN_SMTP_FROM=veris@example.com
# PROVEN_SMTP_TLS=1

# Where notifications actually go. Needed because the demo accounts use a `.demo` domain
# that can never receive mail — without this, mail is composed and shown in the outbox
# rather than sent to an address guaranteed to bounce.
# PROVEN_NOTIFY_TO=you@example.com

# ── Xero: the accounting connector ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Xero does not issue API keys. It is OAuth 2.0, so you register a free app at
# developer.xero.com and get a Client ID plus a Client Secret. The free developer
# account also provisions a DEMO COMPANY holding real invoices, contacts and inventory
# items — so the request, the token exchange, the JSON and the parsing are all real, and
# only the business inside it is Xero's sample data. Same compromise demo-site/site.py
# makes for Discovery, and labelled the same way.
#
# UNSET is a supported state. With no credentials the accounting feed falls back to its
# labelled fixture and the interface says so; nothing raises and no row is rendered live.
#
# The redirect URI is string-compared by Xero on every authorisation, so it must match
# the app registration exactly. Use `localhost`, NOT `127.0.0.1`: Xero's edge WAF returns
# a bare HTTP 403 on any token POST whose body carries the loopback IP literal, which
# happens before OAuth is evaluated and reads misleadingly like a rejected client. The
# name form reaches the identity server; the IP form never does. Verified against the
# live endpoint — see the note in xero.py:redirect_uri().
#
# Because of that, browse the product at http://localhost:8000 rather than the IP. A
# session cookie set on 127.0.0.1 is not sent to a callback on localhost, and the state
# check in /api/xero/callback will correctly refuse the mismatch.
# PROVEN_XERO_CLIENT_ID=your-32-character-client-id
# PROVEN_XERO_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
# PROVEN_XERO_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8000/api/xero/callback
